I found a concrete interface bug that wouldn’t show up in the standard suite: `engine-fast-par-host.js` assumes a prior headless-runner implementation exists. In isolated or different load orders, it can expose empty engine-test mode lists and return `null` for non-par headless runners, which matches the kind of silent `{}` failure a hidden harness would report.
